  "reviewer_notes": "Single application (one water-tube steam boiler on a petrochemical plant). Five models extracted: M1 energy baseline (linear regression), M2 target/goal line, M3 Base 100 efficiency index, M4 index of real use (evaporation ratio ICactual = EActual/P), M5 control charts. Note internal inconsistency in the dependent-variable definition: the paper labels the equation an 'energy baseline' obtained by regression of 'energy consumption and production', yet Equation 3 (E_Actual = mP + b) explicitly defines E_Actual as 'the real steam production' and P as 'the fuel consumption', making steam production the dependent variable and fuel consumption the predictor. Extraction follows the explicit equation-3 definition; dependent quantity coded 'other' (real steam production) with requires-inference. Also note a numeric discrepancy in the target-line R2: the abstract (p.2) states R2 = 0.97 while the results section (p.5) states R2 = 0.9933; the results-section value was recorded for M2. The measurement date range on p.3 gives identical start/end (04-12-2016 and 04-12-2016), an apparent typo; the six-month monitoring period is stated separately (p.2). Data origin ('calibrated sensor') coded as dedicated meter with requires-inference; boundary correspondence inferred exact. No quantified energy-saving result is reported numerically in the text (only qualitative identification of inefficiency peaks).",
